<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle on the Marchfeld</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1278">1278</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Dürnkrut and Jedenspeigen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle on the Marchfeld, also called the Battle of Dürnkrut and Jedenspeigen, was fought on 26 August 1278 on the plain north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf I of Germany</a>, allied with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</a>, defeated and killed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a>. The victory gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, who ruled Austria until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-marchfeld.jpg" alt="Battle on the Marchfeld" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mór Than · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IV_L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_%C3%A9s_Rudolf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
